WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.678 --> 00:00:16.699
stared at the cave door, shocked.

2
00:00:17.859 --> 00:00:18.680
don't believe it.

3
00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:21.761
One-Horned Buffalo stole our weapons again!"

4
00:00:21.841 --> 00:00:24.583
"What will we do now?"

5
00:00:25.043 --> 00:00:26.083
asked the fire god.

6
00:00:28.108 --> 00:00:32.049
"This demon's powers are stronger than any I've seen before," said Wukong.

7
00:00:33.410 --> 00:00:36.730
know one person who can definitely defeat him—Buddha.

8
00:00:37.951 --> 00:00:38.651
I'll be back soon."

9
00:00:39.691 --> 00:00:43.372
The monkey leaped onto a cloud and soared toward the West.

10
00:00:45.873 --> 00:00:48.394
arrived at the Thunderclap Monastery.

11
00:00:49.494 --> 00:00:51.075
A guard at the gate stopped him.

12
00:00:53.155 --> 00:00:55.816
"I need to ask Buddha for help," Wukong told the guard.

13
00:00:56.596 --> 00:00:58.357
"It's about the Tang Monk's journey."

14
00:00:59.758 --> 00:01:01.560
The guard waved the monkey through.

15
00:01:02.440 --> 00:01:05.783
Wukong entered the monastery and bowed before Buddha.

16
00:01:05.803 --> 00:01:08.985
"Greetings, Buddha," said the monkey.

17
00:01:09.005 --> 00:01:12.467
"I need—" held up a hand.

18
00:01:13.228 --> 00:01:15.289
"I know why you're here, Wukong.

19
00:01:16.430 --> 00:01:18.572
also know who the demon is.

20
00:01:19.512 --> 00:01:22.955
You must go to Laozi for help."

21
00:01:23.495 --> 00:01:26.641
"Oh, okay," said the monkey, a bit surprised.

22
00:01:26.661 --> 00:01:27.702
"Thank you."

23
00:01:29.643 --> 00:01:31.344
Wukong flew toward Heaven.

24
00:01:31.364 --> 00:01:35.226
"Laozi doesn't like me much," thought the monkey.

25
00:01:35.246 --> 00:01:37.467
"He won't be happy to see me."

26
00:01:43.570 --> 00:01:47.132
When Wukong arrived at Laozi's house, the sage frowned.

27
00:01:47.152 --> 00:01:49.093
"What do you want, Wukong?"

28
00:01:49.494 --> 00:01:50.254
asked Laozi.

29
00:01:50.274 --> 00:01:53.596
"Buddha told me to come here," said Wukong.

30
00:01:54.284 --> 00:01:57.827
"The Tang Monk was captured by a demon called One-Horned Buffalo."

31
00:01:57.847 --> 00:01:59.508
"Oh dear!"

32
00:01:59.969 --> 00:02:00.729
said Laozi.

33
00:02:00.749 --> 00:02:02.351
"Do you know him?"

34
00:02:02.651 --> 00:02:03.411
asked the monkey.

35
00:02:04.913 --> 00:02:06.674
nodded. "He's my green buffalo.

36
00:02:07.535 --> 00:02:08.956
I didn't realize he'd escaped."

37
00:02:10.697 --> 00:02:13.860
"Well, he did," said Wukong, getting annoyed.

38
00:02:14.740 --> 00:02:16.362
he's planning to eat the Tang Monk.

39
00:02:18.283 --> 00:02:20.125
Your buffalo also has a metal ring.

40
00:02:21.125 --> 00:02:23.908
Every time we try to fight him, the ring sucks in our weapons!"

41
00:02:25.132 --> 00:02:26.653
Laozi held up his hands.

42
00:02:26.673 --> 00:02:28.094
"Okay, okay.

43
00:02:28.974 --> 00:02:30.195
I can capture the buffalo.

44
00:02:30.695 --> 00:02:31.316
Don't worry."

45
00:02:34.117 --> 00:02:36.138
The sage went into another room.

46
00:02:38.340 --> 00:02:40.821
When he came back, he was holding a fan.

47
00:02:40.841 --> 00:02:42.962
"Let's go."

48
00:02:47.425 --> 00:02:49.886
Wukong and Laozi returned to the mountain.

49
00:02:49.906 --> 00:02:53.880
"Buffalo!" shouted Laozi.

50
00:02:53.900 --> 00:02:55.041
"Get out here right now!"

51
00:02:56.422 --> 00:03:00.605
The door flew open, and One-Horned Buffalo stepped outside.

52
00:03:02.066 --> 00:03:04.407
His face fell when he saw Laozi.

53
00:03:05.548 --> 00:03:08.570
Laozi raised the fan and brought it down fast.

54
00:03:11.372 --> 00:03:14.714
A fierce wind nearly knocked over One-Horned Buffalo.

55
00:03:16.595 --> 00:03:20.258
The demon pulled off the metal ring and flung it at Laozi.

56
00:03:22.579 --> 00:03:26.098
The sage caught it and brought the fan down once more.

57
00:03:27.599 --> 00:03:32.123
The wind knocked over the demon, and he turned into a large, green buffalo.

58
00:03:33.424 --> 00:03:35.726
The buffalo stood up and snorted.

59
00:03:37.407 --> 00:03:40.410
Laozi tucked the fan and the ring into his robe.

60
00:03:42.031 --> 00:03:45.834
Then he climbed onto the buffalo and rode up into the sky.

61
00:03:48.537 --> 00:03:52.360
Wukong went into the cave, and the warrior and two gods followed.

62
00:03:54.528 --> 00:03:56.190
They soon found their weapons.

63
00:03:56.210 --> 00:04:00.814
"The gods and I will return to Heaven now," said the warrior.

64
00:04:00.834 --> 00:04:03.356
"Good luck with your journey, Wukong."

65
00:04:03.376 --> 00:04:06.099
"Thank you," said the monkey.

66
00:04:08.501 --> 00:04:11.324
Wukong found his companions deep in the cave.

67
00:04:11.344 --> 00:04:14.607
"What took you so long?"

68
00:04:14.807 --> 00:04:20.192
cried Bajie.

69
00:04:20.352 --> 00:04:24.937
was busy fighting a demon," said Wukong, untying the Tang Monk.

70
00:04:25.017 --> 00:04:27.499
"Thank you, Wukong," said the monk.

71
00:04:28.300 --> 00:04:29.941
"You're welcome," said the monkey.

72
00:04:29.961 --> 00:04:34.185
"But next time I tell you to stay away from a place, please listen!"

73
00:04:36.567 --> 00:04:40.090
A few weeks later, the travelers arrived at a busy city.

74
00:04:41.151 --> 00:04:45.976
The streets were filled with people selling vegetables, spices, and other goods.

75
00:04:47.188 --> 00:04:49.890
An old woman was stirring a large pot of soup.

76
00:04:50.911 --> 00:04:53.172
Other food sizzled over fires.

77
00:04:55.114 --> 00:04:56.094
breathed deep.

78
00:04:56.114 --> 00:05:01.358
"Ah! That smells wonderful!"

79
00:05:03.339 --> 00:05:06.101
Suddenly a young woman rushed out of the crowd.

80
00:05:07.362 --> 00:05:08.022
Tang Monk!"

81
00:05:08.503 --> 00:05:09.063
she cried.

82
00:05:09.784 --> 00:05:11.585
She threw her arms around the monk.

83
00:05:12.445 --> 00:05:17.620
A fierce wind swirled, and a second later they were both gone!
